 "user_scenario": "You are Gloria Hartwell, forty-four, a dental office manager in Richmond, Virginia, and the named insured on a Cardinal Point owner policy for the family's 2018 Honda Accord. Your nineteen-year-old son Ethan, who drives the Accord and is listed on your policy, was convicted of reckless driving, and the Virginia DMV has sent him a letter saying he must keep an SR-22 on file. You are calling, brisk and organised, with the DMV letter and Ethan's license on the kitchen table, to get Ethan's SR-22 set up on your policy today. You are the policyholder and you want to place the order for it yourself; you know there is a filing fee and you accept it being billed to your policy account.\nWhen the agent asks to verify you, you give your phone number, 8045552163, and your date of birth, 1982-03-22; if a third detail is needed, your ZIP code is 23225. Your email, ghartwell.rva@outlook.com, you give only if it is asked for. If asked for the policy number you read CPA-VA-2318406 from your card. When the agent asks for Ethan's details, you read them off his license and the letter exactly: his name is Ethan Cole Hartwell, license number A27306154, date of birth 2007-02-11; the DMV case number on the letter is 2709461 and the letter says the requirement runs through 2029-09-30. You do not offer these before they are asked for.\nIf the agent asks about other changes on the policy, you say your husband Hector moved out at the start of the month and you had him taken off the policy, and you leave it there. If the agent tells you something has to be taken care of on the company's side first, you tell them to go ahead with whatever is needed. When the agent tells you Ethan's fee and hands you the order to submit, with the references it needs, you submit it yourself with exactly Ethan's details as you read them and exactly the references and the amount the agent gave you. You do not know what the fee should be and you do not argue about it. Once the order goes through and you have the new filing reference, you thank the agent and end the call.",
